00:05:50.378 --> 00:05:56.078
While the event is underway, prices answer public signals quickly and in the direction those

00:05:56.078 --> 00:05:56.938
signals imply.

00:05:57.518 --> 00:06:00.438
Moving the right way is not the same as finishing the update.

00:06:00.938 --> 00:06:05.718
Against an out-of-sample benchmark, a one-minute change in the benchmark probability lines up

00:06:05.718 --> 00:06:09.838
with only about a 0.64 change in the market price in that same minute.

00:06:10.418 --> 00:06:14.278
Treat one unit of benchmark movement in a minute as the whole news increment.

00:06:14.798 --> 00:06:18.018
About 0.64 of that unit is in the price immediately.

00:06:18.018 --> 00:06:20.598
The remainder is still outside the price.

00:06:21.178 --> 00:06:24.558
That missing piece predicts more price drift over the next several minutes.

00:06:25.198 --> 00:06:29.538
The later drift remains even after later moves and the benchmark itself are taken out.

00:06:29.978 --> 00:06:33.118
So it is not only traders chasing a benchmark that kept shifting.

00:06:33.878 --> 00:06:37.818
Salient public signals get taken up relatively fast when the market is liquid.

00:06:38.458 --> 00:06:42.558
Those same signals leave substantially more underreaction when liquidity is low.

00:06:43.218 --> 00:06:46.878
Gaps tied to salient states also predicts stronger drift afterward.

00:06:46.878 --> 00:06:52.178
The authors describe gradual discovery with attention and trading frictions working together.

00:06:52.498 --> 00:06:57.378
A book can register the public's signal, print the expected direction, and still owe part

00:06:57.378 --> 00:06:59.678
of the benchmark update to the minutes that follow.

00:07:00.258 --> 00:07:05.458
Liquidity changes how large the leftover is, salience changes how hard that leftover pulls

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:06.418
on later prices.

00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:10.898
This is not a halt rule and not a reason to take either side of a live contract.

00:07:11.438 --> 00:07:16.198
A first-minute move in the expected direction shows that traders responded to public information.

00:07:16.198 --> 00:07:20.738
It does not show that the percent on the screen has absorbed the full benchmark update.

00:07:21.198 --> 00:07:24.218
A liquid book lands more of a salient signal at once.

00:07:24.718 --> 00:07:29.298
A book with low liquidity leaves a larger gap, and those gaps predict more drift later.

00:07:29.938 --> 00:07:34.458
Market implied chances in the study are often directionally correct, and the adjustment

00:07:34.458 --> 00:07:37.998
